  "feature": "experimental-multihop-delegation",
  "$comment": "Chain claims-sibling convention as in del-mh-001 (parallel chain_claims array; __COMPUTED_CHAIN_HASH__). The revocation snapshot stays on the JCS profile in v0.2 (its serialization is unchanged by the JWS migration, though its signing input is not — RFC-AITP-0008 §1.5). Its signature placeholder __VALID_B_SIG__ is minted by B over the JCS-canonical bytes of the INNER `revocation_list` body, never the `{\"revocation_list\": ...}` wrapper.",
  "description": "Multi-hop per-hop revocation (RFC-AITP-0011 §6, aitp/0.3 shape). The chain (identical to del-mh-001) is structurally valid: every hop's JWS verifies, the voucher inside chain[0] verifies under A's own key, continuity, expiry monotonicity, transitive scope subsetting, and chain_hash recomputation all pass. However, B's signed revocation snapshot (B = chain[0].iss) lists chain[0].jti = 550e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655443002 in `entries`. Per RFC-AITP-0011 §6, the verifier MUST look up every hop token's jti against the deny list of that hop's iss (and chain[0].voucher.src_jti against A's own deny list), after all signature checks (RFC-AITP-0008 §3.3); a revocation hit at ANY hop invalidates the entire delegation. Expected: DELEGATION_SOURCE_TCT_REVOKED. Manifest source: `input.issuer_manifests` carries the signed Manifests of both hop issuers, B (kat-keypair-002, chain[0].iss) and C (kat-keypair-003, outer iss); each hop's JWS verifies under the key its issuer's Manifest designates (RFC-AITP-0011 §3 step 1). The voucher needs no Manifest: A verifies it under its own key.",
